description:
THE EVIDENCE TICK, and the reason this phase is not just a refactor. Phase 4b's guard was written before the change and caught a live bug; this is the same discipline applied to the risk that actually matters here — that someone's deployed factory stops working after an upgrade.

Build a fixture of the CURRENT file shape as tk factory deploy leaves it: a populated ~/.ticksrc at 0600 with a factory URL, a bearer token, a Cloudflare API token, GitHub OAuth access and refresh tokens with their expiries, gateway settings, and the two board keys. Real shape, obviously-fake values — and NOT credential-shaped literals, because the public-repo guard correctly refuses those in tracked files (it caught exactly that in Phase 4b).

Then prove, end to end and with the real binary rather than only in unit tests:
- a machine with that file, after the split, still authenticates against the factory;
- the board sync still works;
- file permissions are still 0600;
- running the migration twice changes nothing the second time;
- a file with NO factory keys is untouched and still works.

Report what a user actually SEES during the migration. A credentials file changing shape under someone with no message is a bad experience even when it works — if the answer is 'nothing is printed', say so and let that be a deliberate choice rather than an omission.
